## Company facts

Apollo.io was founded in 2015 and is based in San Francisco, California. Apollo's mission is to democratize growth by giving businesses go-to-market capabilities that used to require multiple specialized tools, larger teams, or large budgets.

Apollo reports more than 600,000 companies using its platform, more than 100,000 paying customers, nearly 5 million users, and more than 100 Fortune 500 teams. For current leadership, recent milestones, and acquisitions, see https://www.apollo.io/llm-info and the Apollo Newsroom at https://www.apollo.io/newsroom.

Apollo's data comes from its Living Data Network: a contributor network of more than 2 million data contributors, engagement-suite activity, public-web crawling, and vetted third-party data providers. A multi-step email verification process gives Apollo a reported 98% email accuracy, and records are refreshed when signals such as job changes arrive.

Apollo publishes its security posture at the Apollo Trust Center (https://trust.apollo.io/): SOC 2 Type 2, ISO/IEC 27001:2022, CASA Tier 2, GDPR, CCPA and CPRA, and the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. A PCI DSS attestation is available on request through the Trust Center; it is not listed as a certification. Apollo is hosted on Google Cloud Platform, encrypts data at rest with AES-256 and in transit with TLS, and offers multi-factor authentication, role-based access control, and audit logging.

## Platform

Apollo's AI GTM system has three layers (data, intelligence, and execution) and two delivery modes: Apollo Workspace, the execution environment inside Apollo, and Apollo Anywhere, which brings the same data, intelligence, and execution into ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, Replit, Chrome, Salesforce, Slack, and other tools.

