## Apollo API

The Apollo REST API lets you search, enrich, create, and manage Apollo data programmatically. All requests go to https://api.apollo.io/api/v1. Apollo users authenticate with an API key sent in the x-api-key header; partners acting on behalf of mutual users use the OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow and send the access token as a Bearer token. Admins, or users with the right permission profile, create keys in Apollo under Settings > Integrations > API Keys. A key only works for the endpoints selected for it unless it is set as a master key.

Rate limits are per team and per endpoint, enforced per minute, per hour, and per day, and they depend on the Apollo plan. Going over a limit returns a 429 status with a retry-after header. Enrichment, organization search, news search, and AI insight endpoints can consume credits; endpoints that create, update, list, or manage records consume 0 credits. The API, MCP, and CLI all follow your Apollo plan, permissions, and credit balance.

- [Build with Apollo](https://docs.apollo.io/docs/build-with-apollo.md): Overview of the ways to build with Apollo: the API, Apollo MCP, and Apollo CLI.
